        "title": "Appeal to definition to rewrite",
        "text": "Dividing by $$\\frac{1}{y}$$ is the opposite of multiplying by $$\\frac{1}{y}$$. But multiplying by $$y$$ is also the opposite of multiplying by $$\\frac{1}{y}$$. Thus dividing by $$\\frac{1}{y}$$ is the same as multiplying by $$y!$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "aaf274fA113-algconseq-P02a-h3",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "aaf274fA113-algconseq-P02a-h2"
        ],
        "title": "Full solution",
        "text": "$$\\frac{\\frac{1}{x}}{\\frac{1}{y}}=\\frac{1}{x} y=\\frac{y}{x}$$",
        "variabilization": {},
